---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "How much does insurance cost and what affects the premium?",
    answer: "Premiums vary by coverage, sum assured, age, health, occupation, and location. Since 22 September 2025, GST has been exempt on individual life insurance and individual health insurance policies, including family floaters and senior-citizen policies. Group policies and other insurance products may be treated differently, so check the insurer's current quote. No Claim Bonus can reduce motor insurance costs.",
    icon: "M5 13l4 4L19 7",
  },
  {
    question: "How do I know which insurance is best for my family and needs?",
    answer: "The best insurance depends on your family size, age, income, existing assets, health conditions, and goals. For families with children, consider term insurance with child riders for education funding. For health coverage, choose between individual and family floater plans based on budget. Motor insurance should include third-party liability and comprehensive coverage. Personal accident insurance is crucial for working adults. I provide personalized advisory based on your unique situation, comparing multiple insurer options to find the most suitable coverage at competitive premiums.",
    icon: "M5 13l4 4L19 7",
  },
  {
    question: "What documents are needed for insurance claims and the process?",
    answer: "Required documents typically include: completed claim form, original policy document, medical reports/invoices (health insurance), FIR and police report (motor theft/accident), death certificate (life insurance), admission letter and bills (hospitalization), doctor prescriptions, and proof of identity/address. The process involves immediate intimation to insurer, claim registration, document submission, verification by insurer, claim settlement, and final disbursement. I can help organize claim documents, prepare submissions, and follow up with the insurer; the insurer makes the claim decision under the policy terms.",
    icon: "M5 13l4 4L19 7",
  },
  {
    question: "Can you help with existing policy review and switching insurers?",
    answer: "Yes, policy review and switching is one of our specialties. We analyze your existing policy for better terms, coverage gaps, and potential savings. Switching can be beneficial if you find better premium rates, higher sum assured, better claim settlement ratio, or more favorable policy terms. We compare multiple insurers using our expertise in policy comparison, ensuring you don't lose continuity of coverage. We handle all the paperwork and coordination with new insurers, ensuring a smooth transition without service gaps.",
    icon: "M5 13l4 4L19 7",
  },
  {
    question: "What is the difference between term insurance and whole life insurance?",
    answer: "Term insurance provides coverage for a specified period (10-40 years) with lower premiums, paying a fixed sum if death occurs during the term. Whole life insurance provides lifelong coverage with premiums that increase with age, includes cash value accumulation, and continues until age 99. Term is suitable for those seeking high coverage at low cost for specific financial goals like children's education or mortgage protection. Whole life is better for those seeking lifelong protection plus an investment component, though premiums are significantly higher. I recommend term insurance for most people, with whole life for those seeking both protection and savings.",
    icon: "M5 13l4 4L19 7",
  },
  {
    question: "How often should I review my insurance policies and with whom?",
    answer: "It's recommended to review insurance policies annually, especially after life changes like marriage, birth of children, career changes, or major financial decisions. Review when changing jobs, relocating, or when insurance companies announce new rates. I offer complimentary reviews for existing clients twice a year, plus free reviews after any major life event. Regular reviews ensure your coverage matches your current needs, identify potential savings through comparisons, discover underinsurance or over-insurance, and ensure claim benefits remain adequate. Professional review is preferred over DIY comparisons for optimal coverage and cost-effectiveness.",
    icon: "M5 13l4 4L19 7",
  },
];
---

<section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-[#0a0a0a] relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10 bg-aurora-grid" />
  <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-[1px] bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-[#10b981]/40 to-transparent" />
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10">
    <!-- Section Header -->
    <div class="text-center mb-16">
      <span class="label-aurora mb-4">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8 10h.01M12 10h.01M16 10h.01M9 16H5a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h14a2 2 0 012 2v8a2 2 0 01-2 2h-5l-5 5v-5z" />
        </svg>
        Common Questions
      </span>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white font-jakarta mb-4" style={{ fontFamily: "'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif" }}>
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] max-w-2xl mx-auto" style={{ fontFamily: "'Inter', sans-serif" }}>
        Get answers to the most common questions about insurance planning and our services.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ Accordion -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <div class="card-aurora">
          <details class="group">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer list-none hover:border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.2)] transition-colors">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white" style={{ fontFamily: "'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif" }}>
                {faq.question}
              </h3>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[#10b981] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-6 pb-6">
              <p class="text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-relaxed" style={{ fontFamily: "'Inter', sans-serif" }}>{faq.answer}</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <!-- More FAQs Link -->
    <div class="text-center mt-12">
      <a
        href="/faq"
        class="btn-aurora-pill"
      >
        View All 50+ FAQs
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 ml-1" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
